# In a loop includes() with a string is one stub call per iteration, with the array and the element that was read. Its result is compared with -1.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[name]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# LOOP-NOT: CallBuiltin
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[index]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[name]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int64 b@{{*}} = Const64(-1
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@[[found]] = NotEqual(b@[[index]], $-1(b@{{*}})
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[found]], Terminal)
# LOOP-NOT: CallBuiltin
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub call is the only call that can throw.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# The stub may write the length, which is read again on every turn: nothing counts the turns ahead of the loop, so the loop polls on each of them.
# CALLS-COUNT-2: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# The counts hold a call, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 11, patchpoints: 3
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 10, patchpoints: 3
